{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Behold. With strength he shall come.</b> It is an epithet of 'hand,' for it is found with masculine form, like והנה בו מגילת ספר (Ezekiel 2:9)." "<b>Behold, his reward.</b> That he gives reward to those who hope for him, and thus his deed is the deed of a hired laborer, and the meaning is the hire of the laborer. But in my opinion this meaning does not cling to the passage; rather, it says that he is not like one seeking hire, and the meaning is: unlike a hired shepherd, therefore כרעה עדרו ירעה — like a shepherd, his flock he shall shepherd."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {1 "The bracketed Hebrew reads כרועה, but the correction note צ״ל indicates כרעה עדרו ירעה; I have followed the corrected reading, which aligns with the sense of the argument."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:08.251405694Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}